<title>USA: Senate committee passes $20 bln energy, water bill.</title>
<headline>Senate committee passes $20 bln energy, water bill.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Senate Appropriations Committee approved a $20 billion spending bill for energy programs, dams and dredging projects in the 1998 fiscal year, up $184 million from 1997, a committee spokesman said Friday.</p>
<p>The committee approved $1.9 billion less than the Clinton administration sought, largely because it did not want to provide money for water projects that would need massive funding in future years which would break a balanced budget.</p>
</text>
